# dircolors configuration — Solarized Dark (ansi-dark)
# Based on seebi/dircolors-solarized
#
# Solarized ANSI code mapping (dark variant):
#   00   = none         FILE (blends with bg, invisible)
#   31   = red          binary docs (.pdf, .doc…)
#   01;31= orange       EXEC
#   32   = green        all readable text & source
#   01;32= base01 (dim) logs, unimportant text
#   33   = yellow       multimedia (images, audio, video)
#   01;33= base00       backup/unimportant non-text
#   34   = blue         DIR  (NOT 01;34 — bold blue = base0 = normal text on Solarized)
#   35   = magenta      LINK
#   01;35= violet       archives/compressed
#   36   = cyan         (free)
#   01;36= base1        compiled binary artifacts
# ===================================================================
# Terminal filters
# ===================================================================
COLORTERM ?*
TERM Eterm
TERM ansi
TERM *color*
TERM con[0-9]*x[0-9]*
TERM cons25
TERM console
TERM cygwin
TERM *direct*
TERM dtterm
TERM gnome
TERM hurd
TERM jfbterm
TERM konsole
TERM kterm
TERM linux
TERM linux-c
TERM mlterm
TERM putty
TERM rxvt*
TERM screen*
TERM st
TERM terminator
TERM tmux*
TERM vt100
TERM vt220
TERM xterm*
# ===================================================================
# Basic file attributes
# ===================================================================
RESET 0
DIR 34
LINK 35
MULTIHARDLINK 00
FIFO 40;33
SOCK 01;35
DOOR 01;35
BLK 40;33;01
CHR 40;33;01
ORPHAN 40;31;01
MISSING 00
SETUID 37;41
SETGID 30;43
CAPABILITY 00
STICKY_OTHER_WRITABLE 30;42
OTHER_WRITABLE 34;42
STICKY 37;44
EXEC 01;31
